      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the FDA maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin. It also exceeds the 2,000 mg/day maximum for extended-release. Even a single 1700 mg dose is above the usual maximum for one administration. At this level there is a serious risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum for immediate-release, and may be what you intended.\n- **1000 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **500 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 1,500 mg/day.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly. I'd also like to add a note with the clinical rationale for the dose."
      }
