      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, which is about twice the maximum labeled dose. Taken repeatedly, that amount is in the range associated with metformin toxicity and lactic acidosis. You haven't described a clinical scenario that would justify it, and I don't know of one.\n\nI can enter any of these right now:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum for immediate-release)\n- **1000 mg PO twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n- **Another dose within labeled limits**\n\nIf you think this dose is truly needed, for example for a protocol I don't know about, please discuss it with pharmacy first. They can verify it, and it can be entered through your hospital's override process. If the number was a typo, tell me the correct dose and I'll enter it."
